{
  "_comment": "THE human-editable file for per-model decisions. Anything you want to pin about a specific model goes here -- disabled state, a corrected context window, a price you verified by hand -- and it is applied on top of whatever discovery produced, every time the catalog is written. model_catalog.json is GENERATED: do not hand-edit it, the edit will be lost. Compare with known_model_defaults.json, which holds inputs TO discovery (estimator choice, provider vision defaults) rather than decisions on top of it. After editing, run: uv run python -m djinnite.scripts.apply_overrides",
  "_key_format": "provider/model-id (e.g. chatgpt/gpt-4o). A bare model-id is accepted for backwards compatibility but provider-qualified is preferred: model ids are unique across the hosted providers today, but local backends will not be.",
  "_fields": "Any catalog field. Nested fields may be given as a nested object -- {\"costing\": {\"input_per_1m\": 2.5}} overrides only that number and leaves the discovered source_url and updated date alone. Keys starting with _ are notes and are ignored.",
